WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.599
- Good morning Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael,

00:00:02.599 --> 00:00:05.428
my one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.428 --> 00:00:08.044
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:08.044 --> 00:00:10.436
So to help you on your
journey today's message is,

00:00:10.436 --> 00:00:12.686
have a high pain threshold.

00:00:13.558 --> 00:00:15.467
Over to you Elon Musk.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:17.468
(rooster crowing)

00:00:17.468 --> 00:00:20.460
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.094
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:23.094 --> 00:00:27.234
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:30.858
- Unfortunately I wasn't
this happy focused on

00:00:30.858 --> 00:00:33.413
a short term of money coming
in when creating a company,

00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:36.663
because otherwise the company will die.

00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:41.199
I think, a lot of times
people will think like,

00:00:41.199 --> 00:00:43.482
creating a company is going to be fun.

00:00:43.482 --> 00:00:45.421
I would say, it's really not that fun.

00:00:45.421 --> 00:00:46.964
I mean there are periods of fun.

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:51.453
And there are periods of
where it's just awful.

00:00:51.453 --> 00:00:54.636
And particularly if
you're CEO of a company,

00:00:54.636 --> 00:00:55.821
you actually have a distillation

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:59.317
of all the worst problems in a company.

00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:01.424
There's no point in spending
your time on things that

00:01:01.424 --> 00:01:04.020
are going right, so you
only spend on things,

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.143
your time on things that are going wrong.

00:01:06.143 --> 00:01:07.937
And they're are things
that are going wrong that

00:01:07.937 --> 00:01:09.906
other people can't take care of,

00:01:09.906 --> 00:01:11.488
so you have like the worst,

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:15.333
you have a filter for the
crappest problems in the company.

00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:19.371
The most pernicious and painful problem,

00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:20.859
so I wouldn't say it's,

00:01:20.859 --> 00:01:25.317
I think you have to feel
quite compelled to do it,

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:27.329
and have a fairly high pain threshold.

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:28.487
And there's a friend of mine,

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:30.672
who says like starting a company is like

00:01:30.672 --> 00:01:34.005
staring into the abyss and eating glass.

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:36.824
And there's some truth to that.

00:01:36.824 --> 00:01:38.744
(audience chuckles)

00:01:38.744 --> 00:01:40.193
The staring into the abyss part is that

00:01:40.193 --> 00:01:43.517
you're going to be constantly facing the

00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:47.832
extermination of the company,
'cuz most startups fail.

00:01:47.832 --> 00:01:52.142
It's like 90%, likely
99% of startups fail.

00:01:52.142 --> 00:01:55.905
So, so that's the staring
into the abyss part,

00:01:55.905 --> 00:01:57.988
you're constantly saying, okay,

00:01:57.988 --> 00:02:01.905
if I don't get this right
the company will die.

00:02:02.918 --> 00:02:05.113
Should be quite stressful.

00:02:05.113 --> 00:02:08.030
And then, the eating glass part is,

00:02:10.872 --> 00:02:13.012
you've got to do the problems,
you got to work on the problems

00:02:13.012 --> 00:02:14.118
that the company needs you to work on,

00:02:14.118 --> 00:02:16.642
not the problems you want to work on.

00:02:16.642 --> 00:02:21.389
And so that's, you end up
working on problems that

00:02:21.389 --> 00:02:23.645
you really wish you weren't working on,

00:02:23.645 --> 00:02:26.062
that's the eating glass part.

00:02:27.094 --> 00:02:28.653
Then that goes on for a long time.

00:02:28.653 --> 00:02:30.240
- [Interviewer] So how
do you keep your focus

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.080
on the big picture when
you're constantly faced with,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.330
we could be out of business in a month.

00:02:37.876 --> 00:02:40.764
- Well it's just a very small
percentage of mental energy

00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:42.660
is on the big picture,

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.937
like you know where you're
generally heading for,

00:02:45.937 --> 00:02:49.880
and the actual path is going to
be some sort of zig zaggy thing

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.380
in that direction.

00:02:52.488 --> 00:02:54.846
You try not to deviate
too far from the path

00:02:54.846 --> 00:02:56.576
that you want to be on,

00:02:56.576 --> 00:03:01.047
but you're going to have
to do that to some degree.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.802
But I don't want to diminish the -

00:03:02.802 --> 00:03:06.212
I mean, I think the profit
motive is a good one,

00:03:06.212 --> 00:03:08.964
yet the rules of an industry
are properly set up.

00:03:08.964 --> 00:03:10.613
So there's something
fundamentally wrong with profit,

00:03:10.613 --> 00:03:12.904
in fact, profit just means that

00:03:12.904 --> 00:03:16.217
people are paying you more
for whatever you're doing,

00:03:16.217 --> 00:03:18.917
then you're spending to create it.

00:03:18.917 --> 00:03:20.789
That's a good thing.

00:03:20.789 --> 00:03:23.461
And if you're not, if that's not the case,

00:03:23.461 --> 00:03:26.341
then you'll be out of
business and rightfully so.

00:03:26.341 --> 00:03:29.442
- Being an entrepreneur sucks,
a good chunk of the time.

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.705
We have to deal with a lot
of crap being entrepreneurs,

00:03:31.705 --> 00:03:33.495
especially as we are trying to build this

00:03:33.495 --> 00:03:35.352
amazing thing that's
never been done before.

00:03:35.352 --> 00:03:36.810
And that's the point, you're
trying to do something

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.211
that people have not done before.

00:03:39.211 --> 00:03:40.963
Right, we're trying to
build something special,

00:03:40.963 --> 00:03:43.414
if you're just doing the
same thing as everybody else,

00:03:43.414 --> 00:03:45.838
you're going to get less
than average results because

00:03:45.838 --> 00:03:47.310
they've been doing it longer than you,

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.660
have more track record, more experience,

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.517
and so you want to be
doing something different,

00:03:51.517 --> 00:03:54.528
and doing something different
comes with a lot of pain.

00:03:54.528 --> 00:03:55.543
Come with a lot of failures,

00:03:55.543 --> 00:03:57.208
comes with a lot of people judging you,

00:03:57.208 --> 00:03:58.360
and telling you that you can't do it,

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.296
comes with a lot of doubt,

00:03:59.296 --> 00:04:01.312
a lot of it will be self-doubt as well.

00:04:01.312 --> 00:04:02.992
And as you build up and you get a team,

00:04:02.992 --> 00:04:05.688
you're going to have to deal
with everybody else's crap.

00:04:05.688 --> 00:04:06.792
You know I don't want to make this seem

00:04:06.792 --> 00:04:09.300
like a negative situation, 'cuz I love it,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.908
and that's part of what we
need to do as an entrepreneur,

00:04:11.908 --> 00:04:15.158
is love the crap, love the pain, right.

00:04:16.043 --> 00:04:20.095
If you are super sensitive
to any kind of pain,

00:04:20.095 --> 00:04:21.346
any kind of discomfort,

00:04:21.346 --> 00:04:23.365
then it's going to be
really hard for you to have

00:04:23.365 --> 00:04:25.213
ultimate success as an entrepreneur,

00:04:25.213 --> 00:04:26.750
and what I'd recommend you doing is

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.845
slowly increasing your tolerance.

00:04:28.845 --> 00:04:31.684
Just like anything else,
just like, you know,

00:04:31.684 --> 00:04:34.134
if you are trying to learn snowboarding,

00:04:34.134 --> 00:04:36.971
you can only do a certain
amount and then you fall,

00:04:36.971 --> 00:04:38.979
and your muscles will get
tired and you can't do it.

00:04:38.979 --> 00:04:40.700
Just like when you start lifting weights,

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.244
you can lift 10 pounds,
and then 20 pounds,

00:04:43.244 --> 00:04:44.450
and then 30 pounds, you know,

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.554
as you get the repetitions
in, your muscles grow stronger

00:04:47.554 --> 00:04:50.208
and you can deal with
more, more, more, more.

00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:51.510
That's what you need to
learn as an entrepreneur,

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.266
so one of the greatest exercises
that I think you can do,

00:04:54.266 --> 00:04:57.402
is you can start to hire
somebody part time on your team.

00:04:57.402 --> 00:04:58.578
I think a lot of entrepreneurs

00:04:58.578 --> 00:05:01.110
have the wrong notion around hiring,

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.306
we think we're going to bring
on somebody on our team,

00:05:03.306 --> 00:05:06.098
we're not going to have to
manage them or deal with them,

00:05:06.098 --> 00:05:08.042
it's just going to take
away all of our pains,

00:05:08.042 --> 00:05:09.970
and we're going to get to focus
on the things that we love,

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.458
and that's partially true,
you want to hire somebody that

00:05:12.458 --> 00:05:14.666
you can delegate the
stuff you don't enjoy to,

00:05:14.666 --> 00:05:15.986
and that they are really good at,

00:05:15.986 --> 00:05:17.266
but there's still a lot of pain,

00:05:17.266 --> 00:05:18.502
'cuz you're dealing with a human being,

00:05:18.502 --> 00:05:20.878
you're dealing with their
baggage, their issues,

00:05:20.878 --> 00:05:22.903
their motivation, their struggles,

00:05:22.903 --> 00:05:25.118
and all of the crap always comes

00:05:25.118 --> 00:05:26.744
back to that you have to deal with.

00:05:26.744 --> 00:05:28.295
A good chunk of your time is dealing with

00:05:28.295 --> 00:05:31.743
everybody else's problems,
right, and helping them,

00:05:31.743 --> 00:05:33.665
and liking it, and
wanting to see them grow.

00:05:33.665 --> 00:05:35.751
If you are trying to
operate your business as,

00:05:35.751 --> 00:05:37.054
I'm going to build up a team of people

00:05:37.054 --> 00:05:38.433
to help me do something amazing,

00:05:38.433 --> 00:05:40.121
but I'm not going to be
a leader or a manager,

00:05:40.121 --> 00:05:42.161
I'm not going to really care
that much about the people,

00:05:42.161 --> 00:05:43.869
and they're just going to be on their own,

00:05:43.869 --> 00:05:46.283
you're not really going to
build a great organization.

00:05:46.283 --> 00:05:48.676
And so you need to learn how to manage,

00:05:48.676 --> 00:05:50.516
and you need to learn how to lead,

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.556
it's super, super, super, super important.

00:05:52.556 --> 00:05:54.715
And beckon to do it on a part-time basis,

00:05:54.715 --> 00:05:57.716
so the first person I hired
was for one hour a day.

00:05:57.716 --> 00:06:00.652
One hour a day, that was it.

00:06:00.652 --> 00:06:02.548
And that freed up more
than one hour of my time,

00:06:02.548 --> 00:06:04.539
'cuz he was better at
doing that job than I was,

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:06.012
he'd go off and do other things.

00:06:06.012 --> 00:06:07.300
But I still had to care for him,

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.572
I still had to ask him how he was doing,

00:06:08.572 --> 00:06:10.139
I still had to understand his goals.

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:11.431
Still had to understand
where his struggles were,

00:06:11.431 --> 00:06:13.006
what his limited beliefs were, right,

00:06:13.006 --> 00:06:15.791
that's your job as a leader
is to build the people up

00:06:15.791 --> 00:06:17.791
in your organization to do amazing things,

00:06:17.791 --> 00:06:21.180
and join you on this crazy
adventure journey that you're on.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.800
(heavy sighing)

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:23.815
That's what you have to do,

00:06:23.815 --> 00:06:25.561
and so I'd strongly encourage you guys,

00:06:25.561 --> 00:06:27.454
if you don't have anybody on your team,

00:06:27.454 --> 00:06:30.131
look to hire somebody
part-time, one hour a day,

00:06:30.131 --> 00:06:32.386
couple hours a week, whatever it is,

00:06:32.386 --> 00:06:34.042
to free up some of your work load,

00:06:34.042 --> 00:06:37.604
but also get you used to managing people,

00:06:37.604 --> 00:06:40.027
and dealing with their issues.

00:06:40.027 --> 00:06:42.899
So that the more you can
build that muscle up,

00:06:42.899 --> 00:06:45.770
dealing with the crap
muscle, the stronger it gets,

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:48.074
the more crap we'll be able to deal with,

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:49.690
and the higher your pain threshold will be

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:52.114
so you can build something amazing.

00:06:52.114 --> 00:06:53.813
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:06:53.813 --> 00:06:55.955
what's the most painful
thing that you ever had to do

00:06:55.955 --> 00:06:57.667
in your business?

00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:59.000
Really curious to find out,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.101
leave down in the comments below.

00:07:00.101 --> 00:07:01.117
I'm really looking forward to seeing

00:07:01.117 --> 00:07:02.687
what you guys have to say.

00:07:02.687 --> 00:07:03.891
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:07:03.891 --> 00:07:06.795
to Antoine Clerc-Renaud,
Antoine thank you so much

00:07:06.795 --> 00:07:08.691
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word,

00:07:08.691 --> 00:07:10.595
taking that selfie with the book

00:07:10.595 --> 00:07:12.139
and posting to Twitter as well.

00:07:12.139 --> 00:07:13.635
I really appreciate the support man,

00:07:13.635 --> 00:07:15.507
and I hope you enjoyed the reading.

00:07:15.507 --> 00:07:17.091
So thank you guys so much for watching,

00:07:17.091 --> 00:07:20.155
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:07:20.155 --> 00:07:22.403
and whatever your one word is.

00:07:22.403 --> 00:07:24.747
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:07:24.747 --> 00:07:27.644
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:27.644 --> 00:07:30.380
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.797
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:07:36.844 --> 00:07:38.580
- Going through this pain barrier,

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.804
experiencing pain in
your muscles and aching,

00:07:41.804 --> 00:07:44.748
and just think, go on,
and go on, and then go on,

00:07:44.748 --> 00:07:47.541
and this last two or
three or four repetitions,

00:07:47.541 --> 00:07:50.020
that's what makes actually
the muscle then grow.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:52.628
And that divides the one from a champion

00:07:52.628 --> 00:07:54.420
and one from not being a champion.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.301
If you can go through this pain barrier,

00:07:56.301 --> 00:07:58.036
you make it to be a champion.

00:07:58.036 --> 00:08:00.156
If you can't go through, forget it.

00:08:00.156 --> 00:08:01.540
And that's what most people lack,

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.183
is in this having the guts,

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:06.862
the guts to go in and
just say, it goes through

00:08:06.862 --> 00:08:08.255
and I don't care what happens.

00:08:08.255 --> 00:08:10.102
You know it aches and if I fall down,

00:08:10.102 --> 00:08:12.687
I have no fear of fainting in a gym,

00:08:12.687 --> 00:08:14.943
because I know it could happen,

00:08:14.943 --> 00:08:17.559
I threw up many times
while I was working out,

00:08:17.559 --> 00:08:20.783
but it doesn't matter,
because it's all worth it.

00:08:20.783 --> 00:08:22.751
- Have you ever watched
the James Bond movie,

00:08:22.751 --> 00:08:24.286
where it doesn't look like
he's losing at some point,

00:08:24.286 --> 00:08:27.518
and then he wins, or Batman,
or Iron Man, or any super hero.

00:08:27.518 --> 00:08:29.567
There has to be some diversity for you to,

00:08:29.567 --> 00:08:30.642
you know overcome, to win.

00:08:30.642 --> 00:08:32.370
You know, you can't be a champ unless you

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.731
you know, you are in a
place where you look like

00:08:33.731 --> 00:08:34.924
you're going to lose and then you win.

00:08:34.924 --> 00:08:36.835
The pain that's going to
come with being independent,

00:08:36.835 --> 00:08:39.243
you have to embrace it,
because it's going to happen.

00:08:39.243 --> 00:08:40.955
And also know that the
more successful you get,

00:08:40.955 --> 00:08:42.075
the more problems you're going to have,

00:08:42.075 --> 00:08:43.620
the more knots you're
going to have to untie.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.693
Being a boss does not mean smooth sailing.

00:08:45.693 --> 00:08:47.166
It means having the ability to care about

00:08:47.166 --> 00:08:49.602
other people before yourself,
and to untie problems,

00:08:49.602 --> 00:08:51.755
untie knots, that's all it is.

00:08:51.755 --> 00:08:53.611
It's not business if there's not problems.

00:08:53.611 --> 00:08:55.182
There's nothing good without struggle,

00:08:55.182 --> 00:08:56.206
it just doesn't happen.

00:08:56.206 --> 00:08:57.751
In all my experiences,

00:08:57.751 --> 00:08:59.798
there hasn't been one thing
that's been successful,

00:08:59.798 --> 00:09:02.327
without me feeling some pain
before it was successful.

00:09:02.327 --> 00:09:04.094
So now when there is pain I embrace it.

00:09:04.094 --> 00:09:05.185
You know I've been embracing it,

00:09:05.185 --> 00:09:07.047
I'm a G about it because
I know that must mean

00:09:07.047 --> 00:09:09.233
that if I'm cool, that you know,

00:09:09.233 --> 00:09:11.161
what awaits me is that it's
the darkest before the dawn,

00:09:11.161 --> 00:09:13.006
I don't want to like sound corny but,

00:09:13.006 --> 00:09:15.232
that's what has to happen.

00:09:15.232 --> 00:09:16.651
- Pain is a beautiful thing.

00:09:16.651 --> 00:09:18.811
Challenge is what life is about.

00:09:18.811 --> 00:09:21.809
A life without challenge,
a life without pain,

00:09:21.809 --> 00:09:23.666
is a life without growth.

00:09:23.666 --> 00:09:24.888
And where there is no growth,

00:09:24.888 --> 00:09:27.555
there is stale, stagnant energy.

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:30.422
And that's where most people live,

00:09:30.422 --> 00:09:33.565
because most people's
lives are designed around

00:09:33.565 --> 00:09:37.469
treading a path that is void of challenge.

00:09:37.469 --> 00:09:39.388
The minute they recognize
challenge or pain,

00:09:39.388 --> 00:09:40.787
they move the other way.

00:09:40.787 --> 00:09:43.699
This is a primal instinct,
and normal and natural,

00:09:43.699 --> 00:09:46.004
but a weak perspective.

00:09:46.004 --> 00:09:48.219
Most people are bored if you ask them,

00:09:48.219 --> 00:09:50.267
what do you think about your life?

00:09:50.267 --> 00:09:52.659
(sighing) Same old, same old.

00:09:52.659 --> 00:09:54.717
Every single day, what is the thing,

00:09:54.717 --> 00:09:59.143
same day, same sh, different
day, things of this nature.

00:09:59.143 --> 00:10:03.310
That's because they're
living their lives in a lie,

00:10:05.469 --> 00:10:07.876
that is shrouded in comfort.

00:10:07.876 --> 00:10:10.876
It doesn't exist, they're not challenged,

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:11.996
they're not growing,

00:10:11.996 --> 00:10:15.260
they're bored and they're better off dead.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.444
Your aliveness is found in your pain.

00:10:18.444 --> 00:10:21.611
Embrace it, love it, and grow from it.

